  "processing": "scripts/process-relics.py",
  "jadeCuts": "tail x < 350 + .10*(y-512) -3; head x > 730 - .10*(y-512) +3; body between; 6px saw gaps. Fragments crop and center; joined retains original coordinates. Celadon edge spill is clamped within 3px of alpha edges, leaving interior pigments unchanged.",
  "names": "10 copies of one generated bamboo master with varied wear/rotation. Only 衡 is typeset in shipped OFL Noto Serif SC; a separate horizontal stroke is at its side. Other names remain illegible incisions.",
  "boneLight": "The incidental generated center fissure is locally retouched (52px-wide mask; nearby grain sampled at horizontal offsets -35 and +55, excluding transparent pixels; OpenCV NORMAL_CLONE gradient blend); two authored branches replace it. The exact branch vertices are also used by the royal/Kunlun gold overlay in RelicStudy.tsx. Silhouette, alpha, polished edges and surrounding pigment are preserved.",
  "rejected": [
    {
      "source": "resources/art-src/references/art-direction-3/birds-rejected.png",
      "reason": "Near wing was intact; feet too lifelike. Replaced with edit_00028_.png."
    }
  ],
